-- title:
--   Attachment of the opposite node annulus to the second chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a natural number $N \neq 0$ with $q \nmid N$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr` (the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ is $(C(X)^q - X)(C(X) - X^q)$), integrality of the two degeneracy maps from level $N$ to level $Nq$, a place specialisation $P$ for these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume $R$ is a model (its two divisor laws and its two cusp laws hold) and satisfies the fixed-order law. Let $K/\mathbb{Q}$ be a finite subextension of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $w$ be a supersingular place of $modularFunctionFieldC\,k\,N$ over $k$ (rational, affine geometric, with $j$-value in the supersingular set), at which $R$ satisfies the value-integrality law: every $f$ in the node ring $R.nodeIntegers\,w$ has $V.evalAt\,f \in A$ for all places $V$ of $modularFunctionFieldBar(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $P.reduceFst\,V = w$. Let $W_0$ be a finite set of places containing $w$ on which the regularity law for $R$ holds. Assume further that every $g$ in $R.nodeIntegersOver\,K\,w$ differs from the image $R.nodeConst\,K\,w\,o$ of some element $o$ of the coefficient subring $A \cap K$ by a non-unit, and that this node ring is local and Noetherian. Let $\varpi$ be an element of $A \cap K$ whose multiples are exactly the elements killed by the restriction of $red$ to $A \cap K$. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain with irreducible element $\pi$, let $\sigma : W \to$ (the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $R.nodeIntegersOver\,K\,w$) be a ring homomorphism with $\sigma(\pi)$ the image of $R.nodeConst\,K\,w\,\varpi$, let $E \geq 1$, and let $\iota$ be a ring isomorphism of that completion with the crossing model $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi^E)$ carrying each $\sigma(o)$ to the constant $o$, and satisfying the two residue-order laws: if the first node residue of $f$ is nonzero of $w$-order $n$ then $\iota(f)$ is congruent to a unit times the $n$-th power of the second coordinate modulo the ideal generated by $\pi$ and the first coordinate, and symmetrically, if the second node residue of $f$ is nonzero of order $n$ at $arithFrobC\,q\,k\,N \cdot w$ then $\iota(f)$ is congruent to a unit times the $n$-th power of the first coordinate modulo the ideal generated by $\pi$ and the second coordinate. Let $c = (x,y)$ be node coordinates at $w$ over $K$ with $xy = (R.nodeConst\,K\,w\,\varpi)^{E_0} u$ for a unit $u$, and assume the second node residue of $x$ is nonzero with order $1$ at $arithFrobC\,q\,k\,N \cdot w$. Finally, let $An'$ be an annulus over $A$ in $modularFunctionFieldBar(Nq)$ whose domain consists exactly of the places $V$ with $P.reduceFst\,V = w$ that are strict neither on the first nor on the second side, whose parameter satisfies $An'.param \cdot y = \varpi^{E_0}$ and whose modulus is $\varpi^{E_0}$. Then, viewing $modularFunctionFieldC\,k\,N$ as an algebra over the residue field of $A$ through $R.redBar$ followed by $k \to modularFunctionFieldC\,k\,N$: for every component chart $C_2$ over $A$ for $modularFunctionFieldBar(Nq)$ with residue target $modularFunctionFieldC\,k\,N$ and every place $x_2$ of $modularFunctionFieldC\,k\,N$ over the residue field of $A$ such that $x_2$ is a node of $C_2$, the valuation ring of $C_2$ coincides with that of $R.R_2$, and for all $f$ in it the $C_2$-residue is nonzero exactly when the $R.R_2$-residue is, with $x_2.ord$ of the former equal to the order of $R.residue_2(f)$ at $arithFrobC\,q\,k\,N \cdot w$, the annulus $An'$ is attached to $C_2$ at $x_2$: the parameter lies in the integers of $C_2$, its residue has $x_2$-order $1$, and for every $f$ in the integers of $C_2$ with nonzero residue and vanishing order at all places of the annulus domain, and every such place $P'$, the element $P'.evalAt\,f \cdot (P'.evalAt\,An'.param)^{-x_2.ord(C_2.residue\,f)}$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there.
--
--   This is the second-side companion of the end-attachment statement for the annulus at a supersingular point of $X_0(Nq)$: it identifies the annulus cut out by the second branch coordinate as an annulus attached to the chart carrying the second Gauss prolongation, at the node matching $w$ under the arithmetic Frobenius twist. It is one of the attachment inputs used by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_componentCharts_annuli_isAttached_of_crossingPresentation`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.exists_componentCharts_annuli_isAttached_of_crossingPresentation), which assembles the charts and annuli of the semistable reduction at level $Nq$ from a crossing presentation of the completed node ring.
